<title>INDIA: Credit Lyonnais cuts India prime rate.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais cuts India prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais will cut its Indian prime lending rate to 16.0 percent per annum from 17.25 percent effective April 25, a bank official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The new rate is exclusive of interest tax, he said.</p>
<p>The rate cut follows measures announced by the Reserve Bank of India to reduce deposit rates in its monetary policy for first half 1997/98 (April-March) released on April 15.</p>
